===== PLAN.md =====
# raffle.fun audit r001

Target `9238b6ce8eb7f768c0dcd0cfcef26e1427a03155`; captured working tree was clean. User authorization is preserved in USER-AUDIT-REQUEST.txt. This is a security assessment, not production remediation or release authorization.

1. Freeze tracked working-tree bytes, five production files, forge-std revision, dependency closure and all build inputs.
2. Provide equal clean source/specification/dependencies to independent fresh contexts; omit historical findings/tests/scanner suppression.
3. Execute 15 required harness/provider cells plus three supplementary reviews. User subsequently requested all five harnesses through a separate Daybreak Blue lane. Claude/Gemini provider-specific prompts and isolated report directories have been delivered for their own authenticated runners. Handoff is not completion.
4. Run isolated deterministic, fuzz, invariant, static and symbolic campaigns; triage every raw scanner alert after sealing cold passes.
5. Reconcile preserved originals by root cause, produce coverage/property matrices and unmet obligations, verify all frozen inputs.

Budgets: up to 35min per OpenAI/Daybreak controller attempt; 3 targeted diagnostics per recurring setup issue, no indefinite retries. Tool commands have individual 60–600s budgets in campaign-plan.json; Echidna 100k calls/sequences per engine-reported semantics, depth 100, 180s, one worker, fixed seeds; symbolic solver budgets declared in its command. Provider handoffs have their own six-hour outer cap and 75min per cell cap. Missing stages invalidate native completion. No service purchases, broadcasts, production edits, publishing or claim of external certification.

Scope overrides upstream default exclusions to include interfaces. Pashov memory is off. Simao evidence is retained before cleanup. Native proof/reproduction obligations stay explicit. Trail of Bits is a declared six-stage aggregate, not the catalog. OpenKritt needs native engine and pinned workflow/resources; unavailable infrastructure remains blocked. Gebal imports are bound to exact native source/context hashes; separate test-inclusive runs may not consume cold reviews.

Integrity: python3 verify-freeze.py before/after each attempt; records stored per attempt. Source archives are hash-bound, retained read-only captures. Models are selected in the runner, fallback disabled; absent response identity stays unknown.
