# Scope

Project raffle.fun, repository `/Users/hishamel-husseini/Documents/projects/raffle-fun`, commit `9238b6ce8eb7f768c0dcd0cfcef26e1427a03155`. No pre-existing working-tree changes. Core: RaffleFactory, Raffle, IRaffleFactory, IRaffle, RaffleConstants. See scope-files.txt. Five production Solidity files, 31 reachable imported dependency files. All imports, clone implementation immutables, callback base authentication, ERC721 ownership, SafeERC20 and guard behavior are part of the dependency review boundary. Versions: OpenZeppelin 5.6.1; Chainlink Contracts 1.5.0; forge-std 37a36ca389095b2f677abb07642634573ba7e265. Lockfile bytes are frozen.

Declared chain is Ethereum; Hardhat config also maintains Sepolia and local 31337. No deployed instance was supplied for scope; bytecode/live deployment comparison is NOT_APPLICABLE for this candidate. Local forks require supported RPC and explicit block; an unconfigured skipped fork is a coverage gap, not a pass. Canonical USDC and Chainlink wrapper are assumptions subject to integration checks; arbitrary prizes/receivers are untrusted.

Compiler families: Foundry profiles default/ci/audit/audit_strict/audit_release share Solidity 0.8.36, Cancun, optimizer 200, viaIR=false; coverage disables optimizer; comparison enables viaIR and optimizer 1000. Capture effective configuration JSON separately for inherited/default metadata. Hardhat default and production profiles each Solidity 0.8.36, Cancun, optimizer 200. Build/test compile targets include scripts and mocks but these are not deployed production scope.

Adjacent checks: SDK ABI generation/typechecks, frontend economics/transaction decisions and tests, subgraph mappings/codegen/tests, local deployment validators, lint/format, gas/size, coverage, package supply-chain. This is bounded integration validation, not a full frontend/cloud audit.

Excluded from cold model contexts: tests, historical audit artifacts/reports, accepted-risk lists, scanner databases, corpora, old whitepaper archives. Full captured original bytes remain in target.tar.gz for test-inclusive deterministic runs and post-seal historical reconciliation. Clean DESIGN.md is newly derived from current README/architecture/state-machine behavior, not findings. Prior exposure: coordinator saw filenames and existing configurations/test harness source while preparing tools; cold supplementary reviewers and cell controllers received only clean contexts. Native harness resources may contain unrelated benchmark vulnerability examples.

Post-capture integration addendum: a free documented public RPC was found and both maintained mainnet/Sepolia fork tests passed at pinned block/hash values. This closes the unconfigured-fork setup gap for those tests, while no live deployed Raffle/Factory candidate was added to scope. See PUBLIC-FORK-VALIDATION.md.
